==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Devil Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Skelecat''' when obtained from the [[Zombie Awakens!]] (may drop on the first stage but guaranteed on the second) and is at level 20.

==Strategy/Usage==
Zombie Cat is meant to be a light version of [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Fish Cat]], as he is weaker but cheaper and faster-recharging. Use him against some of the weaker Red enemies in [[Empire of Cats]].

Despite losing use quickly outside of Empire of Cats, he is included in a few notable [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Horror Movies (Combo)|Horror Movies]]. When combined, these combos can make cats like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Artist]] far more effective as meatshields, by increasing both numbers and quality.

==='''True Form'''===
Sadly, Skelecat's low stats prevent him from being a viable [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie]] unit, despite gaining strength against them and area attack. However, he still has his own use for the [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] combo with [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necromancer Cat]], which can easily be combined with Biohazard to greatly reduce cooldown times of spammable units.

==='''Talents'''===
It is not recommend to invest in any of Skelecat's expensive Talents at all, since they do nothing to an already bad unit. While he has area attack, his very high cost for his low stats and few knockbacks leads to him being outclassed by Island Cat, [[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Fish Cat]] and [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]] in that regard as a general and specialist melee attacker.

However, if you are crazy enough to invest your NP to his Talents, Skelecat has the potential to become a reliably decent defense-based [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] against Red/Zombies. He has 68,040 effective HP against them at Lv.50, and he performs an impressive DPS of 6K against alongside that. His weaken doubles his effective HP against target traits that he hits, which can go up to 136,080 HP at Lv.50!

The best Talents to invest into are both stat buffs (Hp Buff, Attack Buff), and [[Weaken]]. Recover Speed Up serves no purpose whatsoever, since he's already immensely spammable and makes him more of a cash drain to deploy off cooldown, and Resist Slow has its niche filled by Shigong Cat who is Immune to Slow.

Even with this, it is not recommended to invest into any of Skelecats' Talents. His performance against both enemy types is severely outclassed, to the point where even in {{4c}} he faces competition from far better cats. Most notably, [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cat]] and [[Li'l Fish Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Island Cat]] who can match as well as surpass Skelecat's full investment stats in multiple aspects when at high enough +Levels, and better yet stay relevant far later into the game. But he still can be worth investing if you really want more anti-Zombie for {{4c}}, though.

==='''Orb'''===
Skelecat is not worth using Talent Orbs on due to being extremely outclassed, but you can give him a Strong Effect Up vs Zombies if you feel extra generous.

